NTIA's Irregular Terrain Model (ITM), version 1.4
=================================================

The model in this crate (src/itm.rs, and the interface around it in the other
source files) is derived from the ITS Irregular Terrain Model, version 1.4,
created by the Institute for Telecommunication Sciences of the National
Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA), U.S. Department of
Commerce: https://github.com/NTIA/itm (commit 183ad95, 2024-09-24). We
gratefully acknowledge NTIA's creation of the software.

Changes made to it, on 2026-11-11, by Óscar García Amor:

- Translated from C++ to Rust.
- Reduced to area prediction mode: ITM_AREA_TLS_Ex and ITM_AREA_CR_Ex and the
  functions they use. Point-to-point mode, terrain profile handling and the
  DLL interface are not included.
- The integer codes for climate, polarization, siting criteria and mode of
  variability became enums; the error codes became an error type and the
  warning bits a flags type, keeping NTIA's numbers. Inputs that are NaN, and
  infinite inputs where NTIA checks only a lower bound, are refused with the
  error for that input instead of producing a meaningless loss.
- The computation itself is unchanged, down to the order of the operations.

